        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27836</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27836"/>
        <updated>2025-09-15T02:23:20.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This adds Trusted Type info for a number of API. I am working of Firefox. Where possible I have attempted to determine Chrome and Safari data. Where not found I have marked as false. Supporting data for each case linked inline.</p>
<p dir="auto">APIs added</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/SVGAnimatedString/baseVal" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">SVGAnimatedString.baseVal</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WorkerGlobalScope/importScripts" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">WorkerGlobalScope.importScripts()</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerContainer/register" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">ServiceWorkerContainer.register()</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/trusted-types" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">Content-Security-Policy: trusted-types</code></a> - support for setting the allowed trusted type policy names</li>
</ul>]]></content>
